{"output":"I’ll inspect the lock ownership checks and recovery paths, make a focused source fix, then build and run the supplied regression suite with Node 24.\n\nThe Lua scripts check only whether a lock exists, not whether its token matches the worker’s. That lets stale workers remove or replace the current owner’s lock. I’ll restore token checks and move retry-side promotion after validation so rejected retries cannot emit events.\n\nThe fix retains the existing mismatch and missing-lock errors, renewal failure responses, and token “0” administrative bypass. I’m adding a regression test that recovers and reclaims a job, then checks stale operations and the replacement owner’s ability to finish.\n\nThe build passed. The test command could not start because its output redirection was denied; I’ll rerun it directly without a log file.\n\nFixed lock-token validation for job transitions and single/batch renewal. Rejected retries no longer trigger delayed-job promotion. Administrative bypass remains intact.\n\nVerification on Node 24: npm run build, git diff --check, and your regression command plus tests/worker_ownership.redis.test.ts passed. All 272 tests passed; exit code 0. No remaining blockers.","final_output":"Fixed lock-token validation for job transitions and single/batch renewal. Rejected retries no longer trigger delayed-job promotion. Administrative bypass remains intact.\n\nVerification on Node 24: npm run build, git diff --check, and your regression command plus tests/worker_ownership.redis.test.ts passed. All 272 tests passed; exit code 0. No remaining blockers.","exit_code":0,"model":"gpt-6-astra","session_id":"","steps":34,"tool_calls":[{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"git status --short; node -v; printenv REDIS_PORT; ls -a | head -35; find . -name AGENTS.md -not -path './node_modules/*' -not -path './.git/*'","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-bullmq-G7VJT5/2-handwork/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_o